[Result "*"]

 { Welcome to the puzzle section! This is a very important part of the course, as here is where you will be able to put the lessons learned into practice. I would encourage you to work your way through each puzzle set before moving on to the next topic. This way, you will benefit from having the material still fresh in your mind. Every puzzle is linked to the material of the theory chapter. This type of training, where the student works through exercises according to theme, is an effective method for integrating new concepts and moving towards a level of understanding where you can comfortably apply these ideas in your own games. The puzzles will usually begin with a brief prompt that will help to orient you in the position. In those cases where the puzzle is particularly challenging, an extra hint may be provided. Students are recommended to read each prompt before attempting to find the solution. I have tried to approximately order the puzzles from least to most difficult to help students to warm up and get into the flow in each exercise set. Since this ordering is subjective, you will likely find yourself considering some puzzles later on in the section to be easier than earlier examples. In any case, this is a minor point since the educational value will remain similar regardless of the puzzle order. Each section will contain a varying number of puzzles. As this is the first chapter in the course, we will begin with 15 puzzles only. Other chapters will sometimes contain a higher number. Finally, many of the puzzles will include annotations and supporting variations. It is up to each student to decide how much time you wish to spend on this material, but I hope that they will be helpful, especially in those instances where the correct solution was not found. } 1. { -KEY- } -- 
 *

