 { Each side's pawns are arranged primarily along a particular set of colors. Considering this, can you find the best move for Black to increase control over White's weak squares? } 1... { -KEY- } Bg5 $1 { Correct! Any other move and White would be the one with the advantage, due to their kingside space advantage. With this move, Black wants to exchange dark-squared bishops, since after this the e3 square will become indefensible for White. To make matters worse, it is not just a weak square - it is already an outpost. More on this topic in the next chapter! } 2. Bf3 { Challenging Black's knight immediately is the only path to equality. } Ne3 ( 2... Bxc1 3. Bxg4 $11 { is similar to the game. } ) 
